  "_meta": {
    "notes": [
      "Sample operational data for the wildtours-plugin custom tables: customers, vendors, vendor_rates, rates (sell), availability, bookings (+ items, travelers, payments) and settlements.",
      "CPT references ({ \"pwt_safari_schedule\": \"Title\" }, { \"pwt_room_unit\": \"Title\" }, etc.) are resolved to post IDs at import time — run AFTER 12-SEED-DATA.json so the referenced records exist.",
      "vendor_rates.resource_id = 0 means a generic net rate across all resources of that type (matches the plugin admin convention).",
      "Bookings are contextual demos: totals/items/costs are internally consistent, but treat all numbers as illustrative — verify net rates with suppliers before production.",
      "Settlement + items.cost numbers are tuned so the Vendors admin page shows a meaningful 'Outstanding' per vendor (e.g. Ken Vihar ~6,800, Himgiri ~14,600, Panna Gate View settled to zero).",
      "Re-runs are safe: every table row is deduped by its natural key (email, name, booking_number, resource+date, rate key, reference)."
    ]
  },
